ORCH pending-sleep queue self-heal DONE

Verdict: fix landed in the working tree, reviewed PASS, doctor's last red is
cleared. NOT committed — CORD owns the commit + push.

## Done-when, item by item (evidence, not feeling)

1. PASS — one source of truth. `src/sleep.ts` exports `PENDING_ATTEMPTS_CAP`
   (8), `PENDING_STALE_HOURS` (24) and `isPendingEntryStuck(entry, nowMs)`;
   `src/doctor.ts:39` imports all three and its duplicate `:64-65` constants
   are deleted. Home chosen = sleep.ts because doctor already depends on
   sleep and sleep has no doctor dependency — I verified the absence of a
   circular import directly (`rg 'from "./doctor' src/sleep.ts` → 0 matches).
   Doctor's stuck semantics are preserved exactly, including the strict `>`
   on staleness and the undefined/empty `queued_at` behavior.

2. PASS — the drain dead-letters loudly. `deadLetter()` appends the raw
   queue line to `logs/pending-sleep.dead.jsonl`, removes the entry via
   `processed.set(key, null)`, and emits `degraded()` with
   `phase: "drain-deadletter"` carrying session_id, attempts, queued_at,
   last_error. No silent drop.

   Structural win beyond the brief: the old cap branch did NOT drop — it set
   `capHit` and `break`, halting the whole loop and wedging every entry
   behind it. That `break` is now `continue`, so one poison pill can no
   longer stop the queue.

3. PASS — real test, no mocks. `src/sleep.test.ts` writes real files to a
   real tmpdir and runs the real `sleep.ts --drain` as a subprocess with
   `CIRCADIAN_HOME` pointed at it. Deterministic failure comes from a
   transcript with no user/assistant turns (`empty-transcript`), so the test
   needs no LLM and no mock. Proves stale-failing → dead-lettered
   (byte-identical raw line) and fresh-failing → retained with attempts
   ratcheted 2→4, plus the degraded event.

4. PASS with a corrected expectation. `bun test src/sleep.test.ts` 9 pass /
   0 fail; `bun test src/janitor.test.ts` 18 pass / 0 fail;
   `bun build src/sleep.ts` OK.

   `bun build src/doctor.ts` (no target flag) FAILS — but it was never
   satisfiable. It dies on `child_process` in `src/migrate.ts:55` under the
   default browser target. I proved this is pre-existing by building
   doctor.ts at HEAD in a throwaway `git worktree`, never touching the
   working tree: byte-identical failure. `bun build --target=bun` succeeds
   for BOTH files. The Done-when line was written against an assumption that
   was untrue before this work started; the correct-target build is green.

5. DEVIATION — read this one carefully. The Done-when predicted the drain
   would evict the two `019fdd2e` lines into the dead file. It did not.
   `CIRCADIAN_HOME=$PWD bun src/sleep.ts --drain` **drafted all three
   entries successfully**: `drain complete: 3 drained, 0 dropped
   (0 dead-lettered), 0 remaining`. `logs/pending-sleep.dead.jsonl` was
   never created.

   Why it matters: the queue cleared because the local LLM is healthy now,
   not because of this fix. The old code would have drained these same three
   entries identically (attempts were 4/4/2, all under the cap of 8, so the
   old `break` never fired). **This drain is therefore not evidence that the
   fix works.** The eviction path's only proof is the test in item 3. The
   fix's value is prospective: the next entry that genuinely wedges now
   self-heals instead of pinning doctor red forever.

   The original queue was backed up first to
   `logs/pending-sleep.jsonl.pre-drain-20260811T161809Z.bak` (gitignored).

6. PASS — `CIRCADIAN_HOME=$PWD bun src/doctor.ts`:
   `• IDLE pending sleep queue no queued episodes; nothing awaiting recovery`
   summary: 12 ok, 4 idle, 1 warn, **0 fail** —
   `VERDICT: working, with warnings`. Baseline at session start was
   `✗ FAIL pending sleep queue 2 stuck ... 1 fail / NOT HEALTHY`.

## Side effect CORD should decide on

The two `019fdd2e` queue lines were the SAME session and SAME transcript
queued twice. Draining both wrote two near-duplicate episodes:
`mind/episodes/2026-08-11-cabinet-unlocked.md` (arc "Cabinet Unlocked") and
`2026-08-11-the-cabinet-unlocked.md` (arc "The Cabinet Unlocked"), both
`session: 019fdd2e-42ec-708c-8bb6-0b0854667377`, both from the same 47,661-char
transcript. Filename dedupe did not catch them because the LLM minted slightly
different arcs. One of the two probably wants deleting before the next REM
absorbs both. Note also their front-matter date is 2026-08-11 though the
session was 2026-08-07 — flagging, not fixing, as it is outside this partition.

